body:
> @Haroenv Here is my code:
>
> ```tsx
> "use client";
>
> import algoliasearch from "algoliasearch/lite";
> import { InstantSearch, SearchBox, Hits, Configure } from "react-instantsearch";
> import Image from "next/image";
>
> const searchClient = algoliasearch("###", "###");
>
> const Hit = ({
>   hit,
> }: {
>   hit: { id: string; name: string; imageSrc: string; shopId: string };
> }) => {
>   return (
>     <article>
>       <Image
>         src={hit.imageSrc}
>         alt={hit.name}
>         width={100}
>         height={100}
>         className="h-10"
>       />
>       <p>{hit.name}</p>
>     </article>
>   );
> };
>
> const Search = () => {
>   return (
>     <InstantSearch searchClient={searchClient} indexName="indexName" insights>
>       <SearchBox />
>       <Configure hitsPerPage={5} />
>       <Hits hitComponent={Hit} />
>     </InstantSearch>
>   );
> };
>
> export default Search;
> ```

> I've encountered an issue with `hitsPerPage`.
>
> Here's my code:
>
> ```js
> <Configure hitsPerPage={5} />
> ```
>
> TypeScript gives me the following error:
>
> ```
> Type '{ hitsPerPage: number; }' is not assignable to type 'IntrinsicAttributes & PlainSearchParameters'.
> Property 'hitsPerPage' does not exist on type 'IntrinsicAttributes & PlainSearchParameters'.ts(2322)
> ```
>
> Installed packages:
>
> ```
> * `"react-instantsearch": "^7.11.2"`
>
> * `"algoliasearch": "^4.23.3"`
> ```
>
> Any help on resolving this issue would be greatly appreciated!

You can define the following

```tsx
	const configureProps = {
		hitsPerPage: 12,
		// filters: 'price>0',
		// query: initialQuery
	} as ConfigureProps;
...

<Configure {...configureProps} />

```
